# Solve Log — industrial_supply_planning

## Approach
- Read all public data under /app/data.
- Built a monthly MIP in PySCIPOpt:
  - plant open/startup binaries with min-uptime;
  - plant-product campaign setup binaries with qualification, min batch, max output;
  - regular/overtime production with plant capacity, availability factors, min run;
  - raw material purchases with BOM balance, supply caps, take-or-pay contract minimums;
  - plant→DC and DC→customer shipments split by mode (RAIL/TRUCK), with lane capacity, mode capacity, mode minimums, lane minimums, fixed activation costs, product exclusions;
  - DC inventory balance with zero initial inventory, safety stock, product-specific caps, aggregate storage and throughput;
  - customer demand balance with shortage, monthly shortage fraction and horizon fill-rate service constraints;
  - customer-product sourcing share and split-delivery rules;
  - monthly CO2 budget over materials, process and transport.
- Objective minimizes all listed cost components.
- SCIP parameters: gaprel = 0.0005; time limit from ORCLAW_SOLVE_TIME_LIMIT_SECONDS if set (default 300s).

## Execution
- Command: `python /app/submissions/solve.py`
- Solver status: recorded from model.getStatus() (expected optimal or gap/time-limited with incumbent).
- Validation: after solve, extracted solution, checked demand balance, inventory balance, capacity, lane minimums, service rules, share/split rules, CO2 budget, and wrote solution.csv with the required schema (one row per positive decision, zero rows omitted).

## Notes
- All shipment rows carry a mode_id (RAIL for plant_dc, TRUCK for dc_customer) as required by transport_modes.csv.
- Solution values rounded to 8 decimal places.
- If solver times out before optimality, the best incumbent is written.

